.TH LARZ 1 "LarzOS" "LarzOS" "LarzOS Manual"
.SH NAME
larz \- the LarzOS command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B larz
.I verb
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B larz
is the single entry point for running a LarzOS machine: software, the
declarative system spec
.RI ( /etc/larzos/system.lz ),
money, the AI, configuration generations and your fleet. It is a LarzOS\-styled
front end to
.BR apt\-get (8),
.BR larz-system (8)
and
.BR larz-aid (8),
which all remain usable directly.
.SH SOFTWARE
.TP
.B install \fIpkg\fR... , remove \fIpkg\fR... , search \fItext\fR
Add, remove or find software. A package that declares
.B XB-Larz-Price
is metered: the amount is checked against the
.B pkg
budget and charged to the wallet on install.
.TP
.B update , upgrade , list
Refresh lists, update everything, list what is installed.
.SH THIS MACHINE
.TP
.B plan " [\fIsystem.lz\fR] , apply [\fIsystem.lz\fR] , rollback , status"
Preview, converge, undo, and drift for the system spec.
.TP
.B snapshot " [\fIname\fR]"
Save a configuration generation (\fI/etc\fR, package selection, applied spec).
.TP
.B generations
List generations; the current one is marked.
.TP
.B switch " \fIn\fR"
Restore generation \fIn\fR (a pre\-switch snapshot is taken first).
.TP
.B diff " [\fIn\fR]"
Machine vs. the spec, or vs. generation \fIn\fR.
.SH MONEY
The machine has a wallet. AI usage, metered packages and API calls are spends;
they are capped by
.B larz budget
(or a
.B budget
block in system.lz) and receipted under
.IR /var/lib/larzos/wallet .
.TP
.B wallet
Balance, provider and recent ledger.
.TP
.B pay " \fIwho\fR \fIamount\fR [\fInote\fR]"
Send money. With
.B provider = local
this records an entry; a real provider (cryptolarz, larzpay) settles it.
.TP
.B topup " \fIamount\fR"
Credit the local balance.
.TP
.B budget " [\fIcategory\fR \fIamount\fR]"
Show caps and spend, or set a monthly cap for a category
.RB ( ai ", " api ", " pkg ", " cloud ", " transfer ).
.TP
.B spend " [\fIcategory\fR] [\fImonth\fR]"
Spend breakdown.
.SH AI
.TP
.B ai " \fItext\fR"
Ask the OS model router. \fBlarz ai route|serve|models|pull\fR reach
.BR larz-aid (8)
directly.
.TP
.B do " \fB"\fR\fIgoal\fB"\fR"
Ask the OS how to achieve \fIgoal\fR; it proposes commands, you approve, it runs
them (after a snapshot).
.TP
.B explain " [\fIfile\fR]"
Explain a file, or piped command output / an error.
.TP
.B why " \fItopic\fR"
Diagnose from live machine context (e.g. \fBlarz why boot slow\fR).
.TP
.B code " [\fIargs\fR]"
Start Claude Code, Anthropic's terminal coding agent, in the current
directory. Preinstalled (\fBlarz-claude-code\fR); see
.BR larz-code (1).
.TP
.B ask " \fIquestion\fR"
Q&A with this machine's facts as context.
.SH FLEET
.TP
.B fleet " [add|rm \fIname\fR \fIuser@host\fR]"
Manage the node registry
.RI ( /etc/larzos/fleet.toml ).
.TP
.B fleet apply " [\fIname\fR]"
Push this machine's system.lz to a node (or all) and converge it.
.TP
.B fleet run " \fIcmd\fR"
Run a command on every node.
.TP
.B share
Publish a sanitised system.lz to the LarzOS machine hub; prints an id.
.TP
.B adopt " \fIid\fR|\fIurl\fR"
Fetch a shared spec, show the plan, and (on confirm) make this machine it.
.SH OTHER
.TP
.B doctor
Check identity, engine, AI router, packages, wallet, generations, disk, services.
.TP
.B rebrand " [status|apply|restore]"
Re\-assert (or remove) the LarzOS identity.
.TP
.B version
Component versions.
.TP
.B apt " \fIargs\fR"
Pass \fIargs\fR straight to \fBapt\-get\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/larzos/system.lz
The machine, in Larzscript.
.TP
.I /etc/larzos/wallet.toml
Wallet provider and budget defaults.
.TP
.I /var/lib/larzos/generations/
Saved configuration generations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR larz-system (8),
.BR larz-aid (8),
.BR larz-rebrand (8)
